    3414: {
        "name": 'The Tomb of Shohan',
        "desc": 'Once beautiful, this place has been turned into a slaughterhouse by the hands\nof evil beings ... even more blood and dead, rotting flesh.  This place looks\nlike the feeding grounds of beasts and monsters.  The overturned sarcophagus\nof the once powerful King Shohan lies here.  A door leads to the north and a\ndoorway has been hewn to the east.',
        "exits": {
            "n": {"to": 3413, "keyword": 'door north', "isdoor": True},
            "e": 3419,
        },
        "flags": {"dark": True, "indoors": True},
        "sector": 'inside',
        "extra_descs": [('coffin sarcophagus', "Now destroyed ... there is writing on it: 'All hail the new king; we serve\nthe Roch'tar, the Undying One!  Those who decline his worship shall be\nslaughtered!'")],
    },
    3415: {
        "name": 'The Lower Chambers and Tombs of the Undead',
        "desc": 'The stench of death is heavy in these caverns.',
        "exits": {
            "e": 3420,
            "s": 3416,
            "w": 3410,
        },
        "flags": {"dark": True, "indoors": True, "no_recall": True},
        "sector": 'inside',
    },
    3416: {
        "name": 'Entrance to the Lower Chambers',
        "desc": "You can tell that this area wasn't a part of the original construction.\nThe walls have been hewn by a mighty force look as though they were CLAWED.\nThe passage slopes upward here and also continues to the north.",
        "exits": {
            "n": 3415,
            "u": {"to": 3418, "keyword": 'tunnel', "isdoor": True},
        },
        "flags": {"dark": True, "indoors": True, "no_recall": True},
        "sector": 'inside',
        "extra_descs": [('walls', 'Something BIG must have done this job!  There are traces of BLOOD in the\nclaw marks.')],
    },
    3417: {
        "name": 'The Grand Hall of Kings',
        "desc": 'This is the western wing of the Grand Hall of Kings.  Your only exits are to\nthe east and west in this gloomy hallway.',
        "exits": {
            "e": 3422,
            "w": 3412,
        },
        "flags": {"dark": True, "indoors": True},
        "sector": 'inside',
    },
    3418: {
        "name": 'The Shrine of Cristis',
        "desc": 'Different than the rest, this place has not been desecrated.  An altar still\nstands here and the walls show scenes from the life of Cristis the Kind,\na ruler of the outlying regions west of Midgaard.  There is a stone staircase\nleading down.  The Ghost of Cristis the Kind stands here.',
        "exits": {
            "s": 3419,
            "d": {"to": 3416, "keyword": 'staircase', "isdoor": True, "closed": True},
        },
        "flags": {"dark": True, "indoors": True},
        "sector": 'inside',
        "extra_descs": [('ghost cristis', "His rest has been disturbed by evil creatures who have invaded his domain\nand grave.  He holds up a parchment for you to read:\n\n     Hello stranger and last hope for Midgaard and this tomb!\n   This is a plea for aid by a man long since dead from this Earth.\n     The forces of evil have taken control of this tomb and the\n   Kings of old need your aid to free us and deliver us to peace\n   once again.  I think that I alone have been able to appear and\n   communicate with the mortal world.\n     Roch'tar, the reincarnate Vampire, now rules these tombs.\n   You must find and defeat him and his minions!\n     May God bless you on your Quest!"), ('altar', "It stands 2 feet high with the remnants of candle-wax on top.  There is\nan inscription on the side:  'Praise the almighty Cristis the bringer of\ngood and justice to the world.  He who fought the evilest finally is at\npeace.  May the Gods remember him forever ...'")],
    },
    3419: {
        "name": 'The Tomb of Cristis',
        "desc": 'Everything here has simply been destroyed.   Exits lead north and west.',
        "exits": {
            "n": 3418,
            "w": 3414,
        },
        "flags": {"dark": True, "indoors": True},
        "sector": 'inside',
    },
    3420: {
        "name": 'The Lower Chambers and Tombs of the Undead',
        "desc": 'The stench of death is heavy in these caverns.',
        "exits": {
            "e": 3425,
            "w": 3415,
        },
        "flags": {"dark": True, "indoors": True, "no_recall": True},
        "sector": 'inside',
    },
    3421: {
        "name": 'Entrance Chamber to the Grand Hall of Kings',
        "desc": 'Whoever built this place must have been very rich indeed!  Though you did\nenter through a rather small door this place has enough room to hold several\nscore of people.  The floor has a beautifully woven carpet, and the walls are\ncovered in finely crafted tapestries. You can tell that these things must have\nbeen worth much but they have not lasted well throughout the ages.  Massive\ndoors lead off to the south and a large stone staircase leads up.',
        "exits": {
            "s": {"to": 3422, "desc": 'Finely polished oak doors stand to the south.', "keyword": 'oak', "isdoor": True, "closed": True},
            "u": {"to": 3405, "desc": 'You see a large set of stone stairs leading upwards to a small stone door at\nthe top.', "keyword": 'stone trapdoor door', "isdoor": True, "closed": True, "locked": True, "pickproof": True, "key": 3410},
        },
        "flags": {"dark": True, "indoors": True},
        "sector": 'inside',
        "extra_descs": [('letters graffiti', "'Beware here all of man, because past here lies only death.'\n\n    Insho'rkthon brsskra-lehsn Roch'tar\n\nBeneath, there are two criss-crossing scratchmarks in an X formation that\nlook like someone (or something) raked their claws across the wood."), ('oak', "They're HUGE!  They are at least 12 feet tall and about 10 feet wide.\nIf not for one thing they would be perfectly preserved.  There appears\nto be some letters crudely scratched into the wood."), ('staircase stairs', 'Though quite cracked they do look very stable.'), ('tapestry tapestries', "The tapestries were woven into beautiful and exciting scenes of battles\nlong ago.  One on the left your shows the historic battle between Jubal the\nBenevolent and Hroth Kragen's forces that eventually Jubal's army won (of\ncourse)."), ('stone door trapdoor', "It's rather small and looks quite heavy but maybe with some kind of leverage\nyou could move it.  It has a queerly shaped hole that looks big enough\nfor an equally queerly shaped pole to fit inside.  If only you had it!")],
    },
    3422: {
        "name": 'The Grand Hall of Kings',
        "desc": 'A long hallway stretches east and west.  On the southern side of the hall\nthere are many doors, each with the name of a king who has died and is\nentombed here.  The hallway is beautiful yet chilling.  Even though the area\nhas been kept well by acolytes, there remains a stench of the undead.',
        "exits": {
            "n": {"to": 3421, "keyword": 'oak', "isdoor": True, "closed": True},
            "e": 3427,
            "s": {"to": 3423, "desc": "The door has written above it: 'May all the lands thank Crotus the Victor.\nWithout his guidance this kingdom would not have stood.'", "keyword": 'door', "isdoor": True, "closed": True},
            "w": 3417,
        },
        "flags": {"dark": True, "indoors": True},
        "sector": 'inside',
    },
    3423: {
        "name": 'The Shrine of Crotus',
        "desc": 'Mostly rubble, this place used to be the shrine of the famous king Crotus,\nwho saved the northern regions from being overrun by the goblin hordes of\n100 years ago.  If not for him, Midgaard of course would have eventually been\nconquered as well.  Though Crotus was a goodly king, it was rumored that he\nturned to the dark ways in his dying years ... and died an evil man.',
        "exits": {
            "n": {"to": 3422, "keyword": 'door', "isdoor": True, "closed": True},
            "s": 3424,
        },
        "flags": {"dark": True, "indoors": True},
        "sector": 'inside',
    },
    3424: {
        "name": 'The Tomb of Crotus',
        "desc": 'A sarcophagus lies in the middle of the room and seems undisturbed.\nA hole has been knocked into the east wall.',
        "exits": {
            "n": 3423,
            "e": 3429,
        },
        "flags": {"dark": True, "indoors": True},
        "sector": 'inside',
    },
    3425: {
        "name": 'The Lower Chambers and Tombs of the Undead',
        "desc": 'The stench of death is heavy in these caverns.',
        "exits": {
            "s": 3426,
            "w": 3420,
        },
        "flags": {"dark": True, "indoors": True, "no_recall": True},
        "sector": 'inside',
    },
    3426: {
        "name": 'The Lower Chambers and Tombs of the Undead',
        "desc": 'The stench of death is heavy in these caverns.',
        "exits": {
            "n": 3425,
            "e": 3430,
        },
        "flags": {"dark": True, "indoors": True, "no_recall": True},
        "sector": 'inside',
    },
    3427: {
        "name": 'The Grand Hall of Kings',
        "desc": 'You are in the western part of the Grand Hall of Kings.  To the south is a\ndoor and to the east and west the hall continues.',
        "exits": {
            "e": 3432,
            "s": {"to": 3428, "keyword": 'door', "isdoor": True, "closed": True},
            "w": 3422,
        },
        "flags": {"dark": True, "indoors": True},
        "sector": 'inside',
    },
    3428: {
        "name": 'The Shrine of Mitnar',
        "desc": 'Mitnar was a gruesome beast of a man ... he loved battle ... and nothing\nelse.  Warriors did love Mitnar, and all fighting men honored him.\nOn the wall is depicted battle after battle after battle.\nA small opening has been shaped carefully to the east.',
        "exits": {
            "n": {"to": 3427, "keyword": 'door', "isdoor": True, "closed": True},
            "e": 3433,
            "s": 3429,
        },
        "flags": {"dark": True, "indoors": True},
        "sector": 'inside',
    },
    3429: {
        "name": 'The Tomb of Mitnar',
        "desc": 'The wall paintings show men and women warriors alike bowing down to Mitnar,\nprisoners of war being put to the sword by Mitnar, and great heaps of gold\nand weapons under the feet of Mitnar.  Where his coffin was, there is now\nonly a rectangular blemish on the floor of the dusty room.',
        "exits": {
            "n": 3428,
            "w": 3424,
        },
        "flags": {"dark": True, "indoors": True},
        "sector": 'inside',
    },
    3430: {
        "name": 'The Lower Chambers and Tombs of the Undead',
        "desc": 'The stench of death is heavy in these caverns.',
        "exits": {
            "e": 3435,
            "s": 3431,
            "w": 3426,
        },
        "flags": {"dark": True, "indoors": True, "no_recall": True},
        "sector": 'inside',
    },
    3431: {
